  "sourceConflicts": [
    "Nano schematic labels DL1 SMLP34RGB2W3 but assigns common-anode pin 2; ROHM Rev.011 assigns common-anode pin 1. Nets and active-low behavior come from the board diagram; color names come from the official Nano demo Arduino pin14/15/16 and pinned Arduino Nano variant GPIO46/0/45 mapping. This is not a validated package footprint.",
    "Pico official introductory text says GPIO33..37 are used for Octal PSRAM despite identifying an S3R2/2MiB device. The profile uses the exact module capacity and does not claim those pads as independent external I/O.",
    "The public linked MicroPython 4MiB image is a software flash-layout subset; Pico remains a physical 16MiB Flash / 2MiB PSRAM board."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Radio, USB hub/bridge internal behavior and analog electrical properties are unmodeled.",
    "WS2812-class GPIO timing and RGB intensities are digital display policy, not optical calibration.",
    "Nano has no documented physical BOOT button; GPIO0 is an LED channel. No boot control is invented.",
    "Native ROM/LED/BOOT acceptance does not establish browser/WASM or physical-device acceptance.",
